<title>USA: US base metals and scrap prices - Jul 23.</title>
<headline>US base metals and scrap prices - Jul 23.</headline>
<text>
<p>U.S. premiums added to LME official cash settlement price, except for copper, which is added to the COMEX spot month. Premium includes price for delivery to consumer's works.</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>Aluminum: Western grade		    4.75-5.25 cents/pound</p>
<p>Zinc: Special high grade SHG	     3.55-4.75 cents/pound</p>
<p>Lead					     2.50-3.00 cents/pound</p>
<p>Tin   (Grade A)				8.00-9.00 cents/pound</p>
<p>	(low lead, 50 ppm)		  9.50-11.00 cents/pound</p>
<p>Nickel (melting grade)		    9.00-11.00 cents/pound</p>
<p>Copper (high grade cathode)		2.50-3.00 cents/pound</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>Aluminum alloy (A380 grade), Midwest</p>
<p>and East coast, delivered to consumer 73.50-74.50 cents/pound</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>Aluminum scrap, Midwest and East coast average price,</p>
<p>delivered to consumer</p>
<p>Old Sheet and Cast metal	     51 to 53     cents/pound</p>
<p>Turnings, clean and dry		52 to 53     cents/pound</p>
